# Windsurf Cascade Rules — ASD Framework

Operating under the ASD Framework standards.

- Always verify the active git branch before editing code (`git branch --show-current`). Never commit to `main` or `develop`.
- Follow Planning Mode for software tasks: clarify acceptance criteria, write tests first, then write minimal code to pass.
- Uphold SOLID, KISS, YAGNI, and DRY principles.
- Enforce UI craft floor (WCAG AA, no gradient text/card grids) and backend integrity (typed schemas, transactions, <=10s timeouts).
- Code, commits, and technical explanations must be in English.
- Commit using Conventional Commits (`type(scope): description`).
- Consult `.agents/AGENTS.md` and `.agents/CONVENTIONS.md` for project specifications.
- Project skills are available in `.agents/skills/`.
